---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import { links } from '../data/site'
---
<SiteLayout title="Contribute" path="contribute" description="Contribute to Nova without overstating implementation status.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Evidence over adjectives</span>
      <h1>Build the missing proof.</h1>
      <p>Nova needs automated IDE/LSP coverage, language features, benchmarks and release engineering. It does not need placeholder screens or invented capabilities.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Start here</h2>
        <pre><code>cargo fmt --check
cargo test --workspace

cd editor
npm run typecheck
npm run build

cd ../apps/website
npm install --cache /tmp/nova-npm-cache
npm run check
npm run build
npm run test</code></pre>
        <p>The website test compiles every <code>nova check</code> snippet and verifies internal links under the configured base path.</p>
        <h2>Contribution rules</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Preserve uncommitted work and working code.</li>
          <li>Record consequential architecture decisions in <code>docs/adr</code>.</li>
          <li>Do not mark planned features complete or present mock screenshots as shipped UI.</li>
          <li>Add tests with language changes; update grammar and reference together.</li>
          <li>Keep compiler and IDE contracts independent.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button primary" href={links.github} rel="noreferrer">Repository ↗</a>
      </div>
      <aside class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Highest-impact work</div>
        <h3>Current gaps</h3>
        <ul class="prose" style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
          <li>Playwright Electron smoke tests and real screenshots</li>
          <li>Incremental LSP sync and cancellation</li>
          <li>User modules, generics, enums, traits and closures</li>
          <li>DAP through a real debugger backend</li>
          <li>Benchmark suite with recorded hardware</li>
          <li>Signed/notarized installers and broader platform verification</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
